(G) HOW-FAR GAP: largest danger-prob p* for which Shearer Z(lopsided;-p*) > 0
================================================================================
   whole-graph Shearer threshold p* ≈ 0.117077  (vs actual p=1/7=0.142857)
   danger prob would need to SHRINK by factor 1.220x  (band 2/14 -> 2/8.54)
   equivalently the lonely threshold 1/14 would need to be ~1/4.3 to apply.
   TRUE Shearer radius (positivity on ALL induced subgraphs) p** ≈ 0.117077
   => p=1/7 exceeds the Shearer radius by 1.220x. LLL/Shearer cannot apply.

================================================================================
VERDICT
================================================================================
 - The 13 danger events are functions of ONE variable tau, hence never jointly
   independent. LLL/Shearer need NEGATIVE dependency, but the arithmetic forces
   STRONG POSITIVE correlation: divisibility-related runners have overlap up to
   1/14 = 3.5x the independent value 1/49.
 - Symmetric LLL e*p*(D+1)<=1 needs D<=1; actual D=8.  FAILS by 3.5x.
 - Asymmetric/lopsided LLL fixed point DIVERGES (infeasible). FAILS.
 - Shearer's signed independence polynomial is NEGATIVE (Z=-36/343 on the
   lopsided graph); danger prob would need p* (well below 1/7) to certify.
 - ROOT CAUSE: the obstruction is entirely the small consecutive integers 1..13
   whose simple ratios 2:1,3:2,... create heavy positive correlation. The
   7-multiple strangers are globally INDEPENDENT (deg 0) — they are NOT the
   problem; the AP-core is. This matches WHY Riesz/additive-energy methods also
   stall on AP-cores (small additive dimension = high correlation).
 - CONCLUSION: the probabilistic LLL/Shearer route does NOT prove inf L>0. It is
   a clean DEAD-END, but it pinpoints the obstruction exactly (positive correlation
   of the dense small-integer block) and yields the exact overlap law (F).

DONE.
